From 55944aa79cb46158fcbda55c12e837b164fa8eca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:38:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel interfaces: shared SYCL copies and stack
 size checks, Kokkos atomics, empty sets, report of the behaviours

Behaviours and material properties now share the same mechanisms:

- SYCL: the copies of the arrays which are not accessible by the device
  (MFront/GenericParallel/SYCLDeviceCopies.hxx) are used by both
  interfaces. For the material properties, the statistics of an
  asynchronous evaluation are copied if needed, the output is copied to the
  device so that the points where the evaluation fails keep their values,
  a failed allocation is reported, the errors of the kernels are reported
  (wait_and_throw), and any allocation of unified shared memory is
  accessible, as for the behaviours. The behaviours only copy the arrays of
  the variables given variable by variable if a field is copied.
- Stack size of the threads: MFront/GenericParallel/GPUStackSize.hxx and
  MFront/GenericParallel/KokkosStackSize.hxx are used by both interfaces.
  The material properties of the cuda, hip and kokkos backends now check
  the stack size, and honour preserve_stack_size. The kernel is a template
  argument of the function reading its attributes: the CUDA runtime is
  linked statically by default, and a function shared by several libraries
  was resolved to the instance of one library, whose runtime does not know
  the kernels of the other ones (invalid resource handle).
- Kokkos: the synchronous computations of the behaviours use atomic
  operations on a block of Kokkos::SharedSpace, as the material
  properties, instead of a reduction. Both interfaces require
  Kokkos::SharedSpace (static assertion).
- Material properties: the exceptions thrown by the runtimes of the
  backends are reported as runtime errors (-6), as the errors of the CUDA
  and HIP runtimes, whose functions now also catch the exceptions. errno is restored on every return. The number of
  points has the size type in the kernels (int before with CUDA, HIP and
  AdaptiveCpp).
- Empty sets of points are accepted without any check by both interfaces.
- Behaviours: the mfront_gpb_report C function fills an output status from
  the statistics of asynchronous computations, as the report functions of
  the material properties. The synchronous computations use it. With SYCL
  and @SharedData, a null queue is reported as an invalid argument (-2).

Tests: preserve_stack_size (material properties with cuda, hip and kokkos,
behaviours with cuda and hip), SYCL statistics in host memory, SYCL queues
of the behaviours (null, out-of-order), data transfer policy none for the
behaviours (sycl-default-acpp-2), execution of a material property
compiled without runtime checks, empty sets.
